# List filter panel

Use `@webonone/ui-kit` **`SearchInput`**, **`ListFilterTrigger`**, and **`ListFilterPanel`** on any `FeaturePage` that displays a filterable collection (`ItemList` + `ListPageFooter`).

Skill: [.cursor/skills/item-list/SKILL.md](../skills/item-list/SKILL.md) · pagination: [item-list-pagination.mdc](item-list-pagination.mdc) · search primitive: [ui-kit-consumption.mdc](ui-kit-consumption.mdc) · data loading: [redux-store-and-epics.mdc](redux-store-and-epics.mdc).

Reference: `ui-kit/package/src/components/SearchInput.tsx`, `ListFilterPanel.tsx`, `email/frontend/src/features/history/pages/HistoryPage.tsx`.

## When required

- Page shows a paginated or slice-paginated **collection list**
- User can narrow results by search text, status, date, or similar criteria

## Pattern

```tsx
<FeaturePage
  title="…"
  actions={
    <div className="flex w-full flex-wrap items-center justify-end gap-2">
      <SearchInput
        value={searchQuery}
        onChange={(e) => setSearchQuery(e.target.value)}
        onClear={() => setSearchQuery('')}
        placeholder="Context-specific hint"
        aria-label="Search …"
        className="w-64"
      />
      <ListFilterTrigger active={hasActiveFilters} onClick={() => setFilterOpen(true)} />
    </div>
  }
>
  <ListFilterPanel
    open={filterOpen}
    onOpenChange={setFilterOpen}
    onApply={handleApply}
    onClear={handleClear}
  >
    {/* FormField + Select / DatePicker — not text search */}
  </ListFilterPanel>
  <ItemList>…</ItemList>
  <ListPageFooter … />
</FeaturePage>
```

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Search left of filter | `SearchInput` always **before** `ListFilterTrigger` in `actions` |
| Compact on small screens | When `description` is set, actions (Search + filter + CTA) sit on their own row below the wrapping description. Below `sm`, tap the search icon to expand the field leftward across that row (right edge stays on the icon). **`ListAddButton`** shows **+ Add** until tapped, then expands left with the same motion. Dialogs/pickers stay a full field. |
| Right-aligned row | Wrap actions in `flex w-full flex-wrap items-center justify-end gap-2` |
| Forbidden body search on list pages | Do **not** place `SearchInput` as a `FeaturePage` child above the list |
| Text search in header | Use **`SearchInput`** — not plain `Input` / `Label` |
| Panel filters only | Status, dates, MIME type, etc. — not primary text search |
| Filtered date labels | When showing applied date filters in UI, use [date-display-format.mdc](date-display-format.mdc) (`Oct 10, 2026`) |
| No inline filter forms | Do not add full-width `<Form>` rows above lists |
| `active` trigger | `true` when any **panel** filter ≠ default (search is separate) |
| Apply | Reset pagination to page 1; refetch (server) or re-slice (client) |
| Placeholder | Match list domain (`"Company name"`, `"Template name or slug"`, …) |

Search-only pages (no panel filters) may use **`SearchInput` alone**. Dialogs, pickers, and embed bodies that search a list also use **`SearchInput`** (body placement is fine there) — [ui-kit-consumption.mdc](ui-kit-consumption.mdc).

## Exceptions

- Auth, embed chrome, and form-only pages (no collection list)
- Single-card pages (e.g. Providers)
- Media embed routes — search + filter in `ScopedFolderBrowser` toolbar (`SearchInput` still required)

## Verification

```bash
npm run type-check -w <service-root>
```
